sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant FastAPI as GuardrailsApp<br/>Port 8000<br/>No Auth
    participant Rails as LLMRails Engine<br/>Colang Runtime
    participant InputR as Input Rails<br/>Safety Filters
    participant OutputR as Output Rails<br/>Safety Filters
    participant Models as Pre-cached Models<br/>MiniLM/Arctic/spaCy
    participant LLM as LLM Provider<br/>OpenAI / Azure OpenAI<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over Client,LLM: Flow 1: Chat Completion (Full Pipeline)
    Client->>FastAPI: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Content-Type: application/json<br/>config_id: {optional}
    FastAPI->>Rails: Route to config<br/>(by config_id or default)
    Rails->>InputR: Evaluate input rails<br/>(user/system messages)
    InputR->>Models: Embedding similarity check<br/>Jailbreak detection
    Models-->>InputR: Evaluation result
    alt Input blocked
        InputR-->>Rails: BLOCKED
        Rails-->>FastAPI: Blocked response
        FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK (blocked message)
    else Input approved
        InputR-->>Rails: APPROVED
        Rails->>LLM: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>HTTPS/443<br/>Auth: API Key
        LLM-->>Rails: LLM Response
        Rails->>OutputR: Evaluate output rails<br/>(assistant messages)
        OutputR->>Models: Content safety check
        Models-->>OutputR: Evaluation result
        alt Output blocked
            OutputR-->>Rails: MODIFIED/BLOCKED
            Rails-->>FastAPI: Filtered response
            FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK (modified message)
        else Output approved
            OutputR-->>Rails: APPROVED
            Rails-->>FastAPI: Original response
            FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK (LLM response)
        end
    end

    Note over Client,LLM: Flow 2: Guardrail Check Only (No LLM Call)
    Client->>FastAPI: POST /v1/guardrail/checks<br/>{role: "user"|"assistant"|"tool",<br/> content: "..."}
    FastAPI->>Rails: Route by message role
    alt role = user/system
        Rails->>InputR: Evaluate input rails
        InputR->>Models: Safety evaluation
        Models-->>InputR: Result
        InputR-->>Rails: Pass/Fail + details
    else role = assistant
        Rails->>OutputR: Evaluate output rails
        OutputR->>Models: Safety evaluation
        Models-->>OutputR: Result
        OutputR-->>Rails: Pass/Fail + details
    end
    Rails-->>FastAPI: Check result
    FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK (check result)

    Note over Client,LLM: Flow 3: Standalone Checks (Colang 1.0)
    Client->>FastAPI: POST /v1/checks<br/>{messages: [...]}
    FastAPI->>Rails: Evaluate via Colang 1.0
    Rails->>Models: Rail evaluation
    Models-->>Rails: Results
    Rails-->>FastAPI: Check results
    FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK

    Note over Client,LLM: Flow 4: Health Check
    Client->>FastAPI: GET /healthz
    FastAPI-->>Client: 200 OK
